{{Quote|I am Bossk from Trandosha! I did not come to Monad Outpost to die in this arena. But if I am to die tonight, I wish to die as a warrior.|Bossk|<ref name="Gamble">''[[Ezra's Gamble]]''</ref>}}
'''Trandosha''', also known simply as '''Dosh''', was an [[Tree|arboreal]] [[planet]] located in [[the galaxy]]'s [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] and the [[homeworld]] of the [[Trandoshan]] [[species]]. It was [[orbit]]ed by [[Wasskah]], a verdant [[moon]], and was positioned in the [[Kashyyyk system|same]] [[star system]] as [[Kashyyyk]], the homeworld of the Trandoshans' fierce rivals, the [[Wookiee]]s. The feared Trandoshan [[bounty hunter]] [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]] hailed from Trandosha.

==Description==
Also known simply as Dosh,<ref name="Squadrons">''[[Star Wars: Squadrons]]''</ref> Trandosha was a [[planet]]<ref name="Trandosha" /> located in the [[Kashyyyk system]],<ref name="Trandosha location" /> a single-[[star]]<ref name="Trandosha's star" /> [[Star system|system]] positioned in the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim's]] [[Mytaranor sector]].<ref name="Trandosha location" /> It was located in grid square P-9 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Grid Coordinates" /> Trandosha was [[orbit]]ed by [[Wasskah]],<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" /> a [[Color|verdant]] [[moon]],<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> and neighbored the planet [[Kashyyyk]],<ref name="Wookiee">{{Databank|wookiee|Wookiee}}</ref> which shared the same system.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" />

A [[Temperature|temperate]] world of thick [[jungle]]s and [[forest]]s<ref name="Trandosha" /> and plains,<ref name="Tooth and Claw" /> Trandosha was a [[Hunting|hunter's]] paradise.<ref name="Trandosha" /> It had a greenish hue when viewed from [[Realspace|space]], and large, white clouds loomed over the planet's marbled surface.<ref name="Padawan Lost">{{TCW|Padawan Lost}}</ref> Trandosha was the [[homeworld]] of a [[species]] of [[Dog|hound]] known as the [[Trandoshan hunting hound]], which had a squarish [[Mouth|muzzle]], as well as a species of [[jellyfish]] known as the [[Doshian jellyfish]].<ref name="Tooth and Claw" />

==History==
In [[382 BBY]],<ref name="382 Date note">''[[The High Republic: Cataclysm]]'' features the [[Night of Sorrow]], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[382 BBY]].</ref> during the [[Standard week|week]] before the [[Battle of Jedha]], a [[Consulate reception on Trandosha|consulate reception]] was held on Trandosha. The [[Jedi Master]] [[Orin Darhga]] attended the meeting and tried to tell a joke, which he based in toilet humor, unaware that such a statement would end up insulting the locals and invite him open to [[Duel on Trandosha|duel]]. Using his [[lightsaber]] in the clash, Darhga won the subsequent duel but kept the event in his mind to remember toilet humor was not always admired, with the experience also convincing him he was a poor [[ambassador]].<ref name="Cataclysm">''[[The High Republic: Cataclysm]]''</ref>

==Inhabitants==
{{Quote|Back home on Dosh, my clan and I never got along. 'You're too loud, Feresk.' 'Why don't you like hunting, Feresk?' Pfeh. As soon as I could fly, I left.|Feresk Tssat, on his life on Trandosha|<ref name="Squadrons" />}}
Trandosha was the homeworld of the [[Trandoshan]]s,<ref name="Moon" /> [[Sentience|sentient]] [[Reptile|reptilian]] [[humanoid]]s who were renowned for their hunting prowess<ref name="Trandoshan">{{Databank|trandoshan|Trandoshan}}</ref> and allied their world with the [[Galactic Republic]].<ref name="Trandosha" /> They had a fierce rivalry with the [[Wookiee]]s, a sentient species that was native to the neighboring world of Kashyyyk.<ref name="Wookiee" /> Trandosha's culture was built around predation and supremacy, ideals that did not always mesh well with the precepts of the [[Jedi Order]] and made Trandoshan [[Jedi]] rare.<ref name="Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref> Toilet humor was not appreciated on Trandosha, with such remarks coming off as insults instead of as jokes. They further were regarded as an invitation to duel the one who made the remark.<ref name="Cataclysm" />

Trandoshans from Trandosha included [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]],<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> one of the most feared [[bounty hunter]]s in the galaxy;<ref name="Bossk">{{Databank|bossk|Bossk}}</ref> his sister, [[Doshanalawook]], who worked to liberate Wookiees from captivity under the alias of Chainbreaker;<ref name="Tooth and Claw" /> the [[Scavenger|salvage]] [[Starship|ship]] [[captain]] [[Gha Nachkt]];<ref name="Gha Nachkt">{{Databank|gha-nachkt|Gha Nachkt}}</ref> the [[Big game hunter|big-game hunter]] [[Garnac]];<ref name="Garnac">{{SWE|characters|garnac|Garnac}}</ref> and the [[pilot]] [[Feresk Tssat]].<ref name="Squadrons" />

==Locations==
{{Quote|So... Remember when we were on Trandosha and you stopped at that diner? Well, I interfaced with a security droid and it told me that they allow droids in the Resistance!|J-4X, to a droid repair technician|<ref name="Takes from the Galaxy's Edge">''[[Star Wars: Tales from the Galaxy's Edge]]''</ref>}}
Trandosha's sunbaked plains were known as [[the Scorch]]. There, Trandoshans enjoyed basking in the sun's rays and mothers routinely laid their nest-[[egg]]s.<ref name="Tooth and Claw" /> The planet was also the location of a [[Restaurant|diner]] that was visited by [[J-4X]] and a [[Unidentified droid repair technician|droid repair technician]] following the founding of the [[Resistance]]<ref name="Takes from the Galaxy's Edge" /> in the [[Standard year|year]] [[28 ABY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref>

