==Behind the scenes==
"Dosha," the Trandoshan homeworld, was the main setting of the original script for "[[Padawan Lost]],"<ref name="Moon" /> the twenty-first episode of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''{{'}} [[The Clone Wars: Season Three|third season]],<ref name="Episode Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Episode Guide]]''</ref> but this locale was later changed to Wasskah, Trandosha's moon. Although not visited, Trandosha can still be seen in the episode's final version,<ref name="Moon" /> as well in the following episode,<ref name="Episode Guide" /> "[[Wookiee Hunt]],"<ref name="Wookiee Hunt">{{TCW|Wookiee Hunt}}</ref> both of which aired on [[April 1]], [[2011]].<ref name="Episode Guide" /> Trandosha traces its origins to the [[1996]] [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] short story "[[The Prize Pelt: The Tale of Bossk]]," written by [[Kathy Tyers]] and featured in the anthology book ''[[Tales of the Bounty Hunters]]''.<ref name="Prize Pelt">{{StoryCite|story=The Prize Pelt: The Tale of Bossk|book=Tales of the Bounty Hunters}}</ref>

